\value{
\code{go_*()} functions return a graph object;
  \code{add_*()} functions return the modified figure.
}
\description{
The data visualized as scatter point or lines in 3D dimension is set in
`x`, `y`, `z`. Text (appearing either on the chart or on hover only) is
via `text`. Bubble charts are achieved by setting `marker.size` and/or
`marker.color` Projections are achieved via `projection`. Surface fills
are achieved via `surfaceaxis`.
}
\details{
\code{go_scatter3d()} creates a validated graph object (a named list).
\code{add_scatter3d()} creates one and adds it to a figure.


Nested objects are given as named lists or with their constructors, which
are linked from the arguments below. Every property is checked against
the plotly.js schema when the object is created or modified (see
\code{\link{plotly_obj-modify}}). One-sided formulas (\code{~col}) are
evaluated in the data, and then checked, when the trace is added with
\code{add_<trace>()} or \code{add_trace()}.
}
\examples{
mtcars |>
  go_figure() |>
  add_scatter3d(x = ~wt, y = ~hp, z = ~mpg)
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{go_figure}()}, \code{\link{add_trace}()}
}
